    {
      "fieldname": "typst_help",
      "fieldtype": "HTML",
      "label": "Typst Help",
      "options": "<div style=\"line-height:1.5;\">\n  <h4 style=\"margin:0 0 10px;\">Typst Help</h4>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:14px;\">\n    <strong>How Styling Works</strong>\n    <ol style=\"margin:6px 0 0 18px; padding:0;\">\n      <li>\n        In normal builder mode, <code>fieldLabelStyle</code>, <code>fieldValueStyle</code>, and <code>sectionLabelStyle</code> are configured in the Builder and automatically inserted before <code>typst_preamble</code>.\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <code>typst_preamble</code> runs before document content and can override global styles.\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        <code>doc_header</code> defines <code>header_block</code>, and <code>doc_footer</code> defines <code>footer_block</code> for page header/footer setup.\n      </li>\n      <li>\n        In Raw Typst mode, Crispy only injects document data and helper functions. Page setup, styling, header, footer, and layout belong in the Raw Typst code.\n      </li>\n    </ol>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:14px;\">\n    <strong>Raw Typst Helpers</strong>\n    <ol style=\"margin:6px 0 0 18px; padding:0;\">\n      <li>Document data is available as <code>#doc.fieldname</code>.</li>\n      <li>Use <code>crispy_image(\"logo.svg\", width: 20mm)</code> and <code>crispy_block(\"document_title-v1.0\")</code> inside function arguments or other Typst expression contexts.</li>\n      <li>When calling a helper directly from markup, add Typst's markup escape: <code>#crispy_image(\"logo.svg\", width: 20mm)</code> or <code>#crispy_block(\"document_title-v1.0\")</code>.</li>\n      <li><code>crispy_image</code> resolves plain filenames only from the current site's private files assets.</li>\n    </ol>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"margin-bottom:14px;\">\n    <strong>Quick Examples</strong>\n    <ol style=\"margin:6px 0 0 18px; padding:0;\">\n      <li>Preamble: <code>#set text(font: \"Inter\", size: 11pt)</code></li>\n      <li>Header: <code>#let header_block = [#text(weight: 700)[#doc.doctype]]</code></li>\n      <li>Footer: <code>#let footer_block = [#text(size: 8pt)[#doc.name]]</code></li>\n      <li>Raw placement: <code>#place(top + left, crispy_image(\"logo.svg\", width: 20mm))</code></li>\n    </ol>\n  </div>\n\n  <div>\n    <strong>Branding Layers</strong>\n    <div style=\"margin-top:4px;\">\n      In normal builder mode, the letterhead is rendered in the page <code>background</code>, while the logo and QR code are rendered in the <code>foreground</code> layer.\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>"
